      html: "<h2>Free and Pro</h2>\n<p>CleanPhoto&#39;s core is free: every scanner, every view, no limits on how much you scan or review. The difference between Free and Pro comes down to one moment — the delete confirmation.</p>\n<h3>What is always free</h3>\n<p>All three detectors — exact duplicates, similar and burst photos, screenshots — plus the month-by-month Swipe view and all review tools are available to everyone. There is no scan quota, no group cap and no locked category.</p>\n<h3>Deleting in the free version</h3>\n<p>When you confirm a deletion in the free version, a short ad plays first, and the deletion completes after it. That is the entire trade: a few seconds of ad per deletion session, instead of a subscription.</p>\n<h3>What Pro changes</h3>\n<p>Pro removes that step. Deletions run immediately with no ad, which matters most in big cleanup sessions where you confirm group after group. Pro is a subscription with weekly and annual plans, billed through your app store account, and you can cancel anytime from your store subscription settings.</p>\n<h3>Which one fits you</h3>\n<p>If you clean occasionally — a screenshot sweep every few months, a duplicate pass after a holiday — Free does everything you need; the occasional ad costs a few seconds. If you maintain a large library, clean in monthly sessions, or simply want the fastest possible workflow, Pro removes the only remaining point of friction.</p>\n<h3>Either way, the same rules apply</h3>\n<p>Both versions scan entirely on your device, never upload your photos, and never delete anything without your explicit confirmation.</p>\n",
