      date: "2026-09-07",
      html: "<h2>Freeform Crop</h2>\n<p>A screenshot with extra borders, a subject that&#39;s too small in the frame, an image that has to match a platform&#39;s specific aspect ratio — all of these call for cropping. Image Converter uses the system-level crop tool, with an intuitive interface and full functionality.</p>\n<h2>Common Cropping Scenarios</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Remove watermarks or borders</strong>: Screenshots and downloaded images often come with extra borders or white margins. Crop them away.</li>\n<li><strong>Emphasize the subject</strong>: The subject is too small in the photo. Crop out the surroundings to make it stand out.</li>\n<li><strong>Match a platform&#39;s ratio</strong>: Crop to 1:1 (avatars), 4:3 (horizontal banners), 16:9 (video covers), and other standard ratios.</li>\n<li><strong>Adapt to social media</strong>: Turn a landscape photo into 9:16 for Stories, or a portrait photo into 1.91:1 for Weibo / X header images.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed Ratios and Freeform Cropping</h2>\n<p>The app supports two cropping modes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fixed ratio</strong>: Choose a common ratio such as 1:1, 4:3, 16:9, or 9:16. The crop frame locks to that ratio for fast, standard-sized output.</li>\n<li><strong>Freeform</strong>: Drag any of the four corners of the crop frame freely. Ideal for irregular trimming.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Cropping Stays on Your Device</h2>\n<p>Cropping runs locally on your device. Neither the original image nor the cropped result is uploaded to a server. For full details on how your data is handled, see the <a href=\"/en/image-converter/privacy/\">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>\n",
